<title>USA: S&amp;P adds SCI, Footstar to indexes.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P adds SCI, Footstar to indexes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's said Monday it would replace U.S. Robotics Corp in its MidCap 400 Index with SCI Systems Inc, currently a component of the S&amp;P SmallCap 600 Index, after close of trading June 12.</p>
<p>U.S. Robotics is being acquired by 3Com Corp in a merger scheduled to close June 12.</p>
<p>SCI Systems will be replaced in the SmallCap 600 Index by Footstar Inc, a New Jersey-based operator of leased footwear departments in Kmart Corp stores and the mall-based Footaction chain.</p>
<p>SCI Systems is headquartered in Huntsville, Alabama, and makes electronic products for the computer, aerospace, defense, telecommunications and other industries.</p>
